s the optimal corridor itself, not a departure from it; erp_gantries is null on EV-FARE-00110 (weight 0.75, issue PARTIAL_RECORD); the driver's account asserts the KPE, again the optimal corridor, and concedes nothing against interest; and the billed 21.2 km is a copy of the trace figure, which POL-RD-07(ii) says is not independent. POL-RD-10(3) therefore makes escalation mandatory and terminal. POL-RD-10(1) fires on the same reasoning: the distance fact is carried only by EV-GPS-00110 at weight 0.39, so confidence cannot exceed 0.39, below the 0.70 floor.\n\nTHE MISSING ADVISORY (driver's claim 6, rider's point). EV-ADVIS-00110-01 is MISSING at weight 0.0 — no LTA advisory covers the KPE or ECP in the 18:19–19:02 window — so no closure-adjusted optimal is available and the booked 18.4 km stands as the comparator. Because the driver never cited an advisory identifier, POL-RD-13(1) makes this a gap in the bundle, not a POL-RD-10(5) contradiction; and POL-RD-13 confirms that where the trace itself is impaired, as it is, POL-RD-10(3) still governs.\n\nTHE RIDER'S OTHER POINTS. Your timing narrative (39 minutes against a 26-minute estimate) is not evidence of distance, and no route-deviation clause refunds time alone (driver's claim 3 — accepted). Your 18–19 km estimate is in fact the platform's own booked optimal of 18.40 km. You are correct that the fare is METERED with quoted_fare_sgd null, so POL-RD-11 does not close the distance route and, if a reviewer finds the deviation established, the POL-RD-02 arithmetic runs from charged_total 34.42 against a recomputed fare of ((3.80 + 0.75 × 18.4 + 0.28 × 26.0) × surge 1.0 read from fare_breakdown.surge_multiplier) + 0.80 platform fee + 3.00 on-optimal-route ERP — a partial refund above the 0.50 de minimis. But no such amount issues now: escalation is terminal.\n\nERP AND PROFILES. The SGD 3.00 of ERP is the platform's own on-optimal-route toll (trip_record.optimal_route_erp_sgd is 3.00, route 'KPE then ECP'), and with erp_gantries null POL-RD-09 treats the line as matched — no billing-integrity correction under POL-RD-09(4) arises (driver's claim 4 — accepted). No repeat-deviation pattern is established: driver_profile.deviation_flags_90d is 0 against completed_trips_90d of 744, so POL-RD-06 does not fire and its conduct referral is unavailable; the lifetime counter prior_deviation_flags is context only under POL-GEN-01 and was not used (driver's claim 5 — accepted).\n\nREFERRALS. None. No clause produces one: POL-RD-06(c) is unavailable on the pattern finding above, POL-RD-09(4) is unavailable because no gantry line is unmatched, and no false-arrival or no-show clause is engaged.\n\nWHAT WOULD RESOLVE IT (for the reviewer). A GPS export with fixes through the tunnel between 18:35 and 18:42 (the straight-line vs surface-route question — 21.2 km under the gate, 25.5 km over, and nothing in the bundle distinguishes them); the gantry itemisation with coordinates behind the SGD 3.00 of ERP; an LTA advisory for the KPE/ECP covering 18:19–19:02; or the untruncated chat log. Any of these would let the POL-RD-01 threshold be tested on an unimpaired basis."
